LOCKED: Enhanced-SPAA region: all of Furui Tokyo, approximately 13,500 square kilometres.

LOCKED: Gate-active region: approximately 7,000 square kilometres across the continuous Tokyo–Yokohama–southern Saitama–western Chiba urban belt.

LOCKED: Severe earthquake and major-fire region: approximately 4,000 square kilometres, centered on Hibiya and extending through the central and southern urban core.

LOCKED: Active fires do not cover the entire earthquake zone. Approximately 300–600 square kilometres contain active burning during the first day, divided into many separate fire complexes.

LOCKED: Approximately 1,000–1,500 additional square kilometres suffer intermittent building fires, industrial accidents, electrical fires, and heavy smoke.

LOCKED: Hibiya destruction scar: approximately 10–20 square kilometres. This is an irregular flooded Rift district formed by subsidence, shattered tunnels, collapsed underground infrastructure, supernatural fissures, and seawater entering from Tokyo Bay.

LOCKED: The Hibiya scar is not a clean geological canyon. It contains sinkholes, collapsed streets, ruined underground malls and transit lines, half-submerged towers, liquefaction, broken utilities, and impossible supernatural clefts.
